1
00:00:02,500 --> 00:00:07,990
Interlock is a verified memory gate for multi-agent systems.

2
00:00:08,040 --> 00:00:13,530
Scout observes. Sentinel verifies. Runner simulates only when the evidence
supports it.

3
00:00:13,580 --> 00:00:20,000
Scout reads a public Sui balance through Tatum, stores the exact observation,

4
00:00:20,050 --> 00:00:26,470
and writes a signed fact to Walrus Memory. It verifies the recalled content
before activating anything.

5
00:00:26,520 --> 00:00:32,705
The memory ledger is an index, not the memory itself. Each record shows its
author,

6
00:00:32,755 --> 00:00:38,940
scope, hash and Walrus blob. Pending or mismatched records are never active
evidence.

7
00:00:38,990 --> 00:00:43,490
An owner records a policy as an immutable Walrus

8
00:00:43,540 --> 00:00:48,040
constraint. Missing policy always means hold, never implicit approval.

9
00:00:48,090 --> 00:00:53,090
An operator creates one immutable plan with an amount and exposure

10
00:00:53,140 --> 00:00:58,140
in basis points. The plan hash binds every later decision and clearance.

11
00:00:58,190 --> 00:01:04,085
Sentinel enumerates the applicable records, recalls each blob,

12
00:01:04,135 --> 00:01:10,030
verifies namespace, author and hash, and applies fixed integer rules. No
language model decides.

13
00:01:10,080 --> 00:01:15,815
Here, a fifteen percent plan is rejected by a verified ten percent policy.

14
00:01:15,865 --> 00:01:21,600
The decision cites the exact fact and constraint, and the verdict is written
back to Walrus.

15
00:01:21,650 --> 00:01:27,485
The demo harness runs the same plan twice. The unguarded baseline would pass.

16
00:01:27,535 --> 00:01:33,370
The protected path rejects with real citations. Same input, different outcome.

17
00:01:33,420 --> 00:01:39,255
Runner accepts only a final approval with a verified verdict memory.

18
00:01:39,305 --> 00:01:45,140
It mints a sixty second, single use clearance and records one simulation. No
funds move.

19
00:01:45,240 --> 00:01:49,310
Interlock. Verified memory. Enforced decisions.
